From 6adb7400fd9de486b5fb3db799c9fabee1ab5786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adhemerval Zanella <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 13:43:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: Fix static PIE CPU feature detection (BZ 34205)

ARCH_INIT_CPU_FEATURES is called from __libc_start_main before
_dl_relocate_static_pie, so any code it runs must not rely on
relocations being applied yet.  Two issues break this under static PIE:

  1. The cpu_list table held 'const char *name' members, whose
     addresses are not link-time constants under PIE and thus require
     base-relative relocations that are not yet in place.  Replace the
     array of structs with a flat NUL-separated name string and a
     parallel midr array, removing the pointer relocations.

  2. tunable_strcmp pulls in memcmp, which is an IFUNC and is likewise
     unresolved at this point.  Redirect memcmp to __memcmp_generic in
     the aarch64 dl-symbol-redir-ifunc.h and include it from
     csu/libc-start.c.

Checked on aarch64-linux-gnu.

Reviewed-by: Wilco Dijkstra  <Wilco.Dijkstra@arm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6adb7400fd9de486b5fb3db799c9fabee1ab5786)

Only the csu/libc-start.c hunk is carried; the rest does not apply to
release/2.43/master.  On 2.43, 1c9988e525 adds a stack struct to
dl_init_cacheinfo that gcc zeroes with a memset call under
-ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero.  In static PIE that call reaches the
unresolved memset IFUNC and elf/ldconfig segfaults at make install on
x86_64 Intel; the include redirects it to the non-IFUNC memset.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Sanchez <fernando.sanchez@chainguard.dev>
---
 csu/libc-start.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/csu/libc-start.c b/csu/libc-start.c
index 1c58561bce..6e7f6b7054 100644
--- a/csu/libc-start.c
+++ b/csu/libc-start.c
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ uintptr_t __pointer_chk_guard_local attribute_relro attribute_hidden;
 #ifndef SHARED
 # include <link.h>
 # include <dl-irel.h>
+# include <dl-symbol-redir-ifunc.h>
 
 # ifdef ELF_MACHINE_IRELA
 #  define IREL_T	ElfW(Rela)
--
2.51.0

